\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {The FLAIR privacy boundary.} The federation's central contract is visible at a glance: patient-level data never crosses the boundary band, and exactly two things do. \emph  {Code crosses rightward}: a developer trains against MIMIC-CLIF using the FLAIR CLI and ships a containerised model whose task script is SHA-256-stamped, so byte-identical execution at every site is verifiable. \emph  {Aggregate JSONs cross leftward}: each of the 12+ CLIF silos runs the container inside CLIF-WorkBench (no internet, no root, immutable image) and emits only four reports (\texttt  {table1.json}, \texttt  {tripod\_ai.json}, \texttt  {fairness.json}, \texttt  {curves.json}) with cell suppression at $n<10$. The FLAIR aggregator verifies the SHA-256 chain across sites and publishes per-site and pooled metrics on the public leaderboard; the per-site forest plot --- not the pooled scalar --- is the headline signal.}}{6}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:workflow}{{1}{6}{\textbf {The FLAIR privacy boundary.} The federation's central contract is visible at a glance: patient-level data never crosses the boundary band, and exactly two things do. \emph {Code crosses rightward}: a developer trains against MIMIC-CLIF using the FLAIR CLI and ships a containerised model whose task script is SHA-256-stamped, so byte-identical execution at every site is verifiable. \emph {Aggregate JSONs cross leftward}: each of the 12+ CLIF silos runs the container inside CLIF-WorkBench (no internet, no root, immutable image) and emits only four reports (\texttt {table1.json}, \texttt {tripod\_ai.json}, \texttt {fairness.json}, \texttt {curves.json}) with cell suppression at $n<10$. The FLAIR aggregator verifies the SHA-256 chain across sites and publishes per-site and pooled metrics on the public leaderboard; the per-site forest plot --- not the pooled scalar --- is the headline signal}{figure.1}{}}
